The src/native files were extracted from LocalViewer's native conversion code.
Changes include removal of Android/JNI presentation and entry points, portable
C++ interfaces, source-preservation validation, and host build integration.
The conversion option contracts follow StillExport.kt, StillExportQuality.kt,
RawExportControls.kt, and ImageConversionPreferences.kt.

Codec libraries are downloaded or supplied separately and retain their own
licenses and notices: libultrahdr (Apache-2.0/MIT), libjpeg-turbo (IJG/BSD/zlib),
libjxl and skcms (BSD/Apache-2.0 and accompanying dependency notices), libavif
(BSD), libaom (BSD and patent license), LibRaw (LGPL/CDDL), and jxrlib (BSD).
Consult each dependency's license files when distributing binaries and source.

The optional Qt desktop links Qt 6 Widgets (LGPL/GPL/commercial licensing) and
Exiv2 (GPL and accompanying dependency notices). The pinned Ultra HDR CPU-count
helper is adapted in a generated build-tree copy to honor per-conversion thread
budgets; its original licenses and notices are retained.
